# Mix of literal key, call-expression computed key, and $varref computed key in same dict
# [$var: val] uses the VALUE of $var as the key (computed key via variable reference)
# [[call-expr]: val] uses the result of the call as the key (computed key via expression)
# Note: keys are evaluated in parent scope (Key Isolation Invariant),
# so the-key is defined in an intermediate dict before the main dict.

[the-key: "world"]
[
  x: 1
  [[str "y"]]: 2
  [$the-key]: "hello"
]

=== out
Dict({"x": Int(1), "y": Int(2), "world": String("hello")})
